§§ `נספחים`

-- Annex א': the owner's undertaking — apply from התשפ"ה every Ofek Hadash
-- provision on special-education schools (work week, pay, pedagogical
-- instructions), listing the schools; breach may bring sanctions up to
-- revocation of the licence.
DECLARE `undertaking action` IS ONE OF
    `apply Ofek Hadash in the listed schools`

@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p4 akn:att_1__hc_1/p5 akn:att_1__hc_1/p7
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `undertaking action`
DECIDE `the owner applies Ofek Hadash on pain of sanctions` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `apply Ofek Hadash in the listed schools`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "the undertaking: breach may bring sanctions up to revocation of the licence"

-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 The undertaking's title; no rule of its own.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p2 The signatory's identification blanks; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p3 The amended regulation it quotes, encoded at `the school is in Ofek Hadash`.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p6 The signatory's confirmation; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p8 Blank columns for the schools; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p9 Signature block; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p10 Signature blanks; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p11 Signature blanks; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p12 Date blank; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p13 Letterhead; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p14 Letterhead; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p15 Letterhead; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p16 Letterhead; no rule.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1 Annex ב': the form for an academic to join by exception without a teaching certificate (no promotion until certified) — the content of 3.2 and 13.2.2, encoded there.
-- akn:att_3__hc_1 Annex ג': the form for a request to the exceptions committee to leave Ofek Hadash, with the principal's view — the content of section 11, encoded there.
-- akn:att_5__hc_1 Annex ה': the addresses for inquiries; no rule.

-- Annex ד': setting the grade and converting the pay. An existing employee
-- is converted; a new one is placed at grade 1 by education and role, with
-- no conversion; the Ministry alone sets grades.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1/p1 akn:att_4__hc_1/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_3
GIVEN e IS A `school employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is converted rather than placed` e IF
    NOT `is a new teaching employee` e

-- The conversion formula: A = X × (Y + 100%) / 100 — X the pay for
-- conversion, Y the coefficient, A the pay after it.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p6 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p15 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p16 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p17 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_a/p5
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER @desc the conversion coefficient, as a share (0.15 for 15%)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the pay after conversion` x y IS
    x TIMES (1 PLUS y)

-- X for a teacher: March's pay, at 100% by the roles, of the year before
-- joining — integrated salary, the '87, '94, 2001, 2008 and 2011
-- supplements, and the role allowances that do not continue (split,
-- training, in-service, double degree); with no employment in March, the
-- joining month; on leave the year before, September of the joining year.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p5
`the components of a teacher's pay for conversion` MEANS
    LIST "integrated salary", "the '87 supplement", "the '94 supplement",
         "the 2001 supplement", "the 2008 supplement", "the 2011 supplement",
         "split allowance", "training allowance", "in-service allowance", "double degree"

@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p6 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_4
GIVEN `employed in March` IS A BOOLEAN, `on leave the year before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `month for conversion`
DECIDE `the teacher's month for conversion` `employed in March` `on leave the year before` IS
    IF `on leave the year before` THEN `September of the joining year`
    ELSE IF `employed in March` THEN `March of the year before joining`
         ELSE `the joining month`

-- Y for an academic teacher is the table printed as an image on the page
-- and absent from the corpus (a corpus defect): an input. A non-academic
-- with 28 years or more takes it times 0.8; a primary-school teacher in
-- grades 7–9 on a 24-hour base, 12.5% more for that part, and then works the
-- primary week.
-- F-2024-25_tashpah_01-k: the coefficient is itself a percentage, so "will
-- grow by 12.5%" reads as 12.5% of it or as 12.5 points. The reading
-- adopted: 12.5% of the coefficient (Y × 1.125), as written below.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p11
ASSUME `the academic teacher's conversion coefficient` IS A NUMBER
@desc Y for an academic teacher, by status (annex ד's table, printed as an image the corpus does not carry).

@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p12 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p13 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p14
GIVEN `academic Y` IS A NUMBER, `is academic` IS A BOOLEAN, `share in grades 7 to 9 on a 24-hour base` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the teacher's conversion coefficient` `academic Y` `is academic` `share in grades 7 to 9 on a 24-hour base` IS
    (IF `is academic` THEN `academic Y` ELSE `academic Y` TIMES 0.8)
    TIMES (1 PLUS 0.125 TIMES `share in grades 7 to 9 on a 24-hour base`)

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the coefficient grown by 12.5 points` y IS
    y PLUS 0.125

`the two readings of 12.5% differ` MEANS
        `the teacher's conversion coefficient` 0.24 TRUE 1 EQUALS 0.27
    AND `the coefficient grown by 12.5 points` 0.24 EQUALS 0.365
#ASSERT `the two readings of 12.5% differ`

-- A is placed by education and seniority at the grade whose pay is the
-- closest equal or higher; and the 2016 shekel supplement and the 2022 Ofek
-- supplement are added by the grade.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p18 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p19 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_2/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_e akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_e/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p2
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, `grid` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc the salaries of the grades, for the employee's education and seniority, in rising order
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary of the grade placed at` a `grid` IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN s YIELD s AT LEAST a) `grid`
    WHEN s FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST s
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_5
`the supplements paid beside the table salary, by the grade` MEANS
    LIST "the 2016 shekel supplement", "the Ofek 2022 supplement"

-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p7 Letterhead; no rule.
-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p8 Letterhead; no rule.
-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p9 Letterhead; no rule.
-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p10 Letterhead; no rule.
-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_3 A repeat of point 1 above (new academic teachers at grade 1, seniority 1), encoded there.
-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b__cls_4 A repeat of point 2 above (leave the year before), encoded there.

-- Deputies: Y = 20%; X is the pay of a 100% position in March of the year
-- before, without the education allowance, expense refunds, sundry payments,
-- tax gross-up and imputed benefit; on leave at the joining, September.
-- Principals: Y = 15%; X likewise, without expense refunds, yearly
-- payments, gross-up and imputed benefit.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_b/p2
`the first deputy's conversion coefficient` MEANS 0.2

@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p2
`what the first deputy's pay for conversion leaves out` MEANS
    LIST "the education allowance", "expense refunds", "sundry payments", "tax gross-up", "imputed taxable benefit"

-- A first deputy or principal on leave when the reform starts: the pay
-- that would have been paid for September of the joining year; otherwise
-- March of the year before, at 100% by the roles.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p3
GIVEN `on leave when the reform starts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `month for conversion`
DECIDE `the manager's month for conversion` `on leave when the reform starts` IS
    IF `on leave when the reform starts` THEN `September of the joining year` ELSE `March of the year before joining`

@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_b akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_b/p2
`the principal's conversion coefficient` MEANS 0.15

@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p2
`what the principal's pay for conversion leaves out` MEANS
    LIST "expense refunds", "yearly payments", "tax gross-up", "imputed taxable benefit"

-- The worked examples. The deputy: components paid by the position
-- (89.167%) summing to 5,948.93, management allowance 2,143.92 paid at
-- 100%; at a full position 8,815.59. The principal: by the position (140%)
-- 14,630.99, management 6,104.14; at a full position 16,554.84.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p6 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p7 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p8 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p9 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p10 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p11 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p12 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p13 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p14 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p15 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p16 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p17 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p18 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p19 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p20 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p21 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p22 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p23 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p24
`the deputy's components by the position` MEANS
    LIST 4194.9, 139.91, 125.85, 207.83, 287.56, 155.58, 270.10, 567.2
`the deputy's management allowance` MEANS 2143.92
`the deputy's position coefficient` MEANS 0.89167

#ASSERT sum `the deputy's components by the position` EQUALS 5948.93
#ASSERT sum `the deputy's components by the position` PLUS `the deputy's management allowance` EQUALS 8092.85
#ASSERT TRUNC (sum `the deputy's components by the position` DIVIDED BY `the deputy's position coefficient` PLUS `the deputy's management allowance` PLUS 0.005) 2 EQUALS 8815.59

@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p6 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p7 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p8 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p9 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p10 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p11 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p12 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p13 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p14 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p15 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p16 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p17 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p18 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p19 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p20 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p21 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p22 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p23
`the principal's components by the position` MEANS
    LIST 8954.48, 219.66, 268.63, 443.63, 613.84, 244.27, 560.01, 3326.47
`the principal's management allowance` MEANS 6104.14

#ASSERT sum `the principal's components by the position` EQUALS 14630.99
#ASSERT sum `the principal's components by the position` PLUS `the principal's management allowance` EQUALS 20735.13

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_01-j: the annex states no rounding. The principal's
-- full-position X, 14,630.99 / 1.4 + 6,104.14 = 16,554.847…, is printed
-- truncated, 16,554.84; but the next line's 17,117.71 is 1.034 times the
-- UNROUNDED X (16,554.84 × 1.034 is 17,117.70). The reading adopted: no
-- rule for the agora; the conversion is computed exactly.
`the principal's full-position X computed` MEANS
    (sum `the principal's components by the position` DIVIDED BY 1.4)
    PLUS `the principal's management allowance`

`the principal example truncates X and carries it unrounded` MEANS
        TRUNC `the principal's full-position X computed` 2 EQUALS 16554.84
    AND TRUNC (`the principal's full-position X computed` PLUS 0.005) 2 EQUALS 16554.85
    AND TRUNC (16554.84 TIMES 1.034 PLUS 0.005) 2 EQUALS 17117.70
    AND TRUNC (`the principal's full-position X computed` TIMES 1.034 PLUS 0.005) 2 EQUALS 17117.71
#ASSERT `the principal example truncates X and carries it unrounded`

-- F-2024-25_tashpah_01-i: both examples then multiply the full-position
-- pay by 1.034, an "erosion supplement" (תוספת שחיקה) — 8,815.59 × 1.034 =
-- 9,115.32 and 16,554.84 × 1.034 = 17,117.71 — before applying the formula,
-- giving A = 10,938.38 and 19,685.37. The formula the annex states (A = X ×
-- (Y+100%)/100), and its definition of X, have no such factor: on them the
-- deputy's A is 10,578.71 and the principal's 19,038.07. The reading
-- adopted: the formula as stated; the 1.034 is read as a factor the annex
-- does not ground.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p25 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_c/p26 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_d akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_d/p2
`the deputy's A as printed` MEANS 10938.38

@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p24 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_c/p25 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_d akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_d/p2
`the principal's A as printed` MEANS 19685.37

`the examples apply an erosion factor the formula does not have` MEANS
        NOT (TRUNC (`the pay after conversion` 8815.59 `the first deputy's conversion coefficient` PLUS 0.005) 2 EQUALS `the deputy's A as printed`)
    AND TRUNC (`the pay after conversion` 9115.32 `the first deputy's conversion coefficient` PLUS 0.005) 2 EQUALS `the deputy's A as printed`
    AND TRUNC (`the pay after conversion` 17117.71 `the principal's conversion coefficient` PLUS 0.005) 2 EQUALS `the principal's A as printed`
#ASSERT `the examples apply an erosion factor the formula does not have`

-- Placement in the examples: the deputy at level 8, grade א, 17,716.63;
-- the principal at level 3, grade א+, 20,086.68.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_2__subpara_e/p3
`the deputy's new integrated salary` MEANS 17716.63
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p3
`the principal's new integrated salary` MEANS 20086.68

#ASSERT `the deputy's new integrated salary` AT LEAST `the deputy's A as printed`
#ASSERT `the principal's new integrated salary` AT LEAST `the principal's A as printed`

-- The principal's personal supplement for the scope above 100% (to
-- 140%): T the full pay by the actual scope in March before; B = T × (100+Y)
-- /100; C = B less the new table salary, turned into a percentage of the
-- integrated salary. In the example: 20,735.13 × 1.15 = 23,845.40, less
-- 20,086.68 = 3,758.72, 18.712%.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p6 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p7 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p8 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p9 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p10 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p11 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p12 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p13 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p14 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p15 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e/p16
GIVEN t IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER, `new table salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the personal supplement rate` t y `new table salary` IS
    (t TIMES (1 PLUS y) MINUS `new table salary`) DIVIDED BY `new table salary`

@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e__cls_1 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e__cls_1/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e__cls_2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e__cls_2/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e__cls_3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e__cls_3/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e__cls_4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_3__subpara_e__cls_4/p2
`the principal's T` MEANS 20735.13

#ASSERT TRUNC (`the principal's T` TIMES 1.15 PLUS 0.005) 2 EQUALS 23845.4
#ASSERT TRUNC (`the personal supplement rate` `the principal's T` 0.15 `the principal's new integrated salary` TIMES 100 PLUS 0.0005) 3 EQUALS 18.712

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Examples on the encoding.
`a primary teacher aged 55` MEANS
    `school employee` WITH
        `post`                                  IS `teacher`
        `stage`                                 IS `primary special-education school`
        `teaches grades 1 to 6`                 IS TRUE
        `has recognised years of actual teaching` IS TRUE
        `is academic`                           IS TRUE
        `holds a teaching certification`        IS TRUE
        `seniority in teaching`                 IS 30
        `age`                                   IS 55
        `position fraction`                     IS 0.5
        `is an intern`                          IS FALSE

`a post-primary health therapist in a multi-stage school` MEANS
    `school employee` WITH
        `post`                                  IS `health-professions employee`
        `stage`                                 IS `multi-stage special-education school`
        `teaches grades 1 to 6`                 IS FALSE
        `has recognised years of actual teaching` IS FALSE
        `is academic`                           IS TRUE
        `holds a teaching certification`        IS FALSE
        `seniority in teaching`                 IS 0
        `age`                                   IS 28
        `position fraction`                     IS 0.25
        `is an intern`                          IS FALSE

